        "y1": 0.5353038995593249
      },
      "text": "APPEAL OUTCOMES",
      "html": null,
      "level": 1,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7559518609854925,
        "y0": 0.5242169404554039,
        "x1": 0.9194608887306056,
        "y1": 0.5875672593806791
      },
      "text": "these categories as some cases concerned more than one subject (for example they may have related to both destitution and further submissions). 3 Judicial review.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "table",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.0676056148744448,
        "y0": 0.5443894095428143,
        "x1": 0.7354370073713706,
        "y1": 0.6390502322156102
      },
      "text": "Q1 Q2 Q3 Q4 2016/17 2015/16 % Allowed 57 57 55 % Remitted 15 15 16 % Dismissed 25 25 25 % Other 3 3",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7570723496327754,
        "y0": 0.5883583365997933,
        "x1": 0.8433062982549272,
        "y1": 0.5978607656582213
      },
      "text": "3 Judicial review.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7553924566083632,
        "y0": 0.5982574920714108,
        "x1": 0.9228206747794301,
        "y1": 0.6422062264666405
      },
      "text": "This figure is adjusted to take into consideration clients whose appeals were withdrawn or who didn’t attend their hearings.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.06831620962377116,
        "y0": 0.650520851892765,
        "x1": 0.9054623401581788,
        "y1": 0.6944695862879948
      },
      "text": "The vast majority of cases that were remitted were appeals against discontinuation decisions. A decision to remit in these circumstances means that the appellant will keep their support so we consider this to be a successful outcome. By adding this proportion to our allowed appeals, our ‘success rate’ was 71%.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "heading",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07055550702531263,
        "y0": 0.708723229875637,
        "x1": 0.20158716292946466,
        "y1": 0.720601266198672
      },
      "text": "APPEAL SUBJECT",
      "html": null,
      "level": 1,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.08231475819619807,
        "y0": 0.7217890698309755,
        "x1": 0.7139545353751874,
        "y1": 0.7372305170509211
      },
      "text": "78% of cases related to Section 4 (s4) support; 22% of cases related to Section 95 (s95) support.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.06775512535361748,
        "y0": 0.7360427134186176,
        "x1": 0.9312201399014911,
        "y1": 0.7807825250329615
      },
      "text": "l appeals were marginally more likely to be dismissed (27% of s95 cases were dismissed compared with 24% of s4 cases). We believe this difference was due to the fact that the majority of s95 appeals related to complex destitution appeals. TOP 5 ISSUES IN Q1: 2",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "heading",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.06943501837802969,
        "y0": 0.779199182791101,
        "x1": 0.21838609317358673,
        "y1": 0.7918694841368825
      },
      "text": "TOP 5 ISSUES IN Q1:2",
      "html": null,
      "level": 1,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07055550702531263,
        "y0": 0.7922650227464396,
        "x1": 0.5846027724954476,
        "y1": 0.8084987349891316
      },
      "text": "1. s4 regulation 3(2)(e) – further submissions cases (72 cases = 46% caseload):   64% allowed, 19% dismissed, 17% remitted",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.08623394862215175,
        "y0": 0.8084987349891316,
        "x1": 0.37629603746833407,
        "y1": 0.8211678485312808
      },
      "text": "64% allowed, 19% dismissed, 17% remitted",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.08567454424502248,
        "y0": 0.8207723099217238,
        "x1": 0.8539450607785297,
        "y1": 0.8374015607739729
      },
      "text": "87% of appeals were allowed where further submissions had been rejected and the JR? was at pre-permission stage",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.08567454424502248,
        "y0": 0.8354214921189229,
        "x1": 0.8920231959628812,
        "y1": 0.863137702075093
      },
      "text": "We won 56% of appeals where the client was preparing further submissions but these had not been handed to the Home Office further 16% of these cases were also remitted. yet.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.08623394862215175,
        "y0": 0.8793702265141526,
        "x1": 0.36733716796914373,
        "y1": 0.8920405278599342
      },
      "text": "70% allowed, 23% dismissed, 2% remitted",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.08455405559773954,
        "y0": 0.8928327928826807,
        "x1": 0.9099426148542862,
        "y1": 0.9229234222998254
      },
      "text": "s4 and s95 destitution cases had different outcomes; 81% of s4 destitution appeals were allowed compared with 55% of s95. This reflects our experience that s95 cases have been getting increasingly complex and difficult to prepare. 3. s4 regulation 3(2)(a): reasonable steps cases (8 cases = 5.1% caseload):",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.06887561400090043,
        "y0": 0.9205478150352184,
        "x1": 0.5549241024331572,
        "y1": 0.9367815272779104
      },
      "text": "3.s4 regulation 3(2)(a): reasonable steps cases (8 cases = 5.1% caseload):",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.08623394862215175,
        "y0": 0.935989262255164,
        "x1": 0.302380744394197,
        "y1": 0.9490551022105026
      },
      "text": "62.5% allowed, 37.5% dismissed",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
